{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/prometheus-adapter","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:11.057Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/cbl-mariner/base/prometheus-adapter/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/cbl-mariner/base/prometheus-adapter/about"},"readme":"***Warning: Azure Linux 2.0 will reach its End of Life (EOL) on July 31st, 2025. After this date, it will no longer receive updates, security patches, or support, which could leave your systems vulnerable. We strongly recommend upgrading to an Azure Linux 3.0 image before July 31st, 2025.***\n\n## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Prometheus-Adapter image for CBL-Mariner.\n\n### What is CBL-Mariner?\n\nCBL-Mariner is an internal Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. CBL-Mariner is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about CBL-Mariner, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Prometheus-Adapter?\n\nPrometheus-Adapter is a project that implements the Kubernetes Custom, Resource, and External Metric APIs in such a way that they integrate Prometheus metrics logging, allowing Kubernetes clusters to easily use Prometheus-Adapter for logging and monitoring.\n\nSee: [https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prometheus-adapter/blob/master/README.md](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prometheus-adapter/blob/master/README.md).\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `0`\n- `0.10`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to Prometheus-Adapter version, Mariner build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running a Prometheus-Adapter container (Assuming an existing Kubernetes project)\n\n`1.` Run the CBL-Mariner Prometheus-Adapter container image with custom config file mounted.\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/base/prometheus-adapter:0.10 <input params>\n\n    docker run -it mcr.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/distroless/prometheus-adapter:0.10 <input params>\n    \nThe container entrypoint is `adapter`, so the user needs to supply arguments like the config file, etc.\n\n## Support\n\nCBL-Mariner container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe CBL-Mariner distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/2.0/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/cbl-mariner/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-07-21T16:51:42.8537055+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"202K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"0.10-cm2.0","digest":"sha256:a0315c2807e3691c14a700e3ce707035d94e4a6fee21f507e28922563e520e4b","pushed":"2026-03-12T22:00:13.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"0.10","digest":"sha256:a0315c2807e3691c14a700e3ce707035d94e4a6fee21f507e28922563e520e4b","pushed":"2026-03-12T22:00:03.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.dock